# Security headers for every page and file of the web app. Cloudflare
# (Workers static assets) reads this file from build/client, and the API sends
# the same `/*` headers when it hosts the app itself (SERVE_STATIC=true).
#
# The Content-Security-Policy line is added to the built copy of this file
# after each build (client/security-headers.ts): it names the API's origin
# from VITE_API_BASE_URL and the hashes of the page's inline scripts, which
# change with every build. docs/security-headers.md explains each header.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
